 "defect_observations": [
  "radon-nikodym annex (readonly host) lines 628-633 and 653-659 assert the integrals of 2x-1 and 1/x by 'direct one-variable integration' and 'monotone integration', and give the mass of [1/n,1) as log n; the value log n is not proved on the route (the owned file proves the sufficient bound n-1), and the annex does not cross-reference thm:p15-w02c-p15-001-signed-density-values / -reciprocal-density. A cross-reference there is a change to a readonly host (lead).",
  "The owned annex proofs annex:p15-w02c-p15-001-lebesgue-rectangles and -stieltjes-notation depend on thm:p15-w02c-p15-002-sigma-finite-uniqueness, and the owned body cites thm:p15-w02c-p15-005-*, def:p15-w02c-p15-005-jensen-direction and thm:p15-w02c-p15-003-block-integrals; those labels live in other packets' unrouted w02c files, so routing must include them or the references dangle.",
  "The owned body (line 744-745) says no fundamental theorem of calculus is proved in this part, while handbook/annex/p15/convolution-gamma-normal.tex lines 7-9 and the product-measures annex (annex:p15.fubini-failures) evaluate integrals by antiderivatives through the fundamental theorem of elementary calculus; the two statements about the calculus background should be reconciled.",
  "conditional-expectation.tex (lines 228-234) and regular-conditional-laws.tex (lines 113-119) use the dx notation before its only definition, which is in the owned file routed later (after w02b-p15-005); a forward cross-reference would help.",
  "integration-expectation.tex lines 378-407 (C018), 426-444 (C020), radon-nikodym.tex lines 85-101 (C006) and 144-172 (C009), conditional-expectation.tex 352-374 (C020) and regular-conditional-laws.tex 31-53 (C002) differ from the recorded exact_current_text; the ledger evidence is stale for these entries."
 ],
